{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790540458,"nonce":"xaglQcOOVlxTO1LtYEGzn+oLZ/E=","title":"wasm: run the scheduler's integration tests on host fibers","message":"caribou's tasks suspend on wasm now: a linked program lends the scheduler Ash's guest fibers (caribou-runtime fiber.rs, sched::host_fiber), and the driver links every wasm program with Ash's fiber transform. That is checked by programs (a two-thread ping-pong over Locks, which only interleaves if a waiting task suspends, under caribou run on wasm32-wasip1 and -threads and in Chrome), but the scheduler's own integration tests still carry #![cfg(not(wasm))] (docs/building.md), because a cargo test binary for wasm is linked by rust-lld, not by Ash's linker, so it gets no transform and no host fibers.\n\nTo run them: link the wasm test binaries through Ash's linker with the transform (ash_wasm_link with LinkOptions.fibers), install host fibers in the test harness as caribou-runtime does, and run them under ash-wasm-run, which drives the transform's globals. Then drop the cfg and the building.md note.","files":null}]}